From: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: size HTC WMI endpoints from the QMI radio count

Before SERVICE_READY selects a hardware mode, single-chip MLO firmware
already reports its PHY count over QMI. HTC still connected one WMI
endpoint per hardware maximum radio and divided the credits between
them, so services were requested for PHYs the IPQ5332 does not have.

Use the QMI radio count when the firmware supports single-chip MLO and the
count is within the hardware maximum; keep the maximum otherwise.

Signed-off-by: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/htc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/htc.c
@@ -773,7 +773,16 @@ int ath12k_htc_init(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 		htc->wmi_ep_count = 3;
 		break;
 	default:
-		htc->wmi_ep_count = ab->hw_params->max_radios;
+		/* Before SERVICE_READY selects a mode, single-chip MLO FW
+		 * already reports its PHY count through QMI. Do not connect
+		 * nonexistent WMI services or divide credits for them.
+		 * Legacy/invalid counts retain the hardware maximum fallback.
+		 */
+		if (ab->single_chip_mlo_support && ab->qmi.num_radios > 0 &&
+		    ab->qmi.num_radios <= ab->hw_params->max_radios)
+			htc->wmi_ep_count = ab->qmi.num_radios;
+		else
+			htc->wmi_ep_count = ab->hw_params->max_radios;
 		break;
 	}
 
